---
title: "vesca_boost - veSCA Earning Boost Calculation (Scallop Lend)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_get_vesca: get user veSCA balance
    q_get_vesca --> q_get_supply: get total veSCA supply
    q_get_supply --> q_get_user_amount: get user supply amount in pool
    q_get_user_amount --> q_get_pool_amount: get total pool supply amount
    q_get_pool_amount --> q_calc_weight: earning_weight = min(user_amount, adjusted_by_vesca_share)
    q_calc_weight --> q_calc_boost: earning_boost = earning_weight / base_weight
    q_calc_boost --> q_check_min: check earning_boost >= 1.0
    q_check_min --> q_cap: earning_boost = max(1.0, earning_boost)
    q_cap --> q_check_max: check earning_boost <= max_boost (e.g. 5x)
    q_check_max --> q_apply: earning_boost = min(earning_boost, max_boost)
    q_apply --> q_calc_apr: earning_apr = pool_incentive_apr * earning_boost
    q_calc_apr --> [*]: return earning_apr

    note right of q_calc_weight
        INV-001: earning_boost minimum is 1.0x (100% = base earning)
        INV-002: more liquidity supplied requires more veSCA for same boost
        INV-003: boost is proportional to veSCA share of total supply
    end note

    note right of q_calc_apr
        INV-004: earning_apr = pool_incentive_apr * earning_boost
        INV-005: boost refreshes on borrow, supply, repay, stake, or extend actions
        INV-006: manual refresh available via "Refresh Boost" button
    end note
